{"version":"2.0","class":"dataset","label":"Orders in industry, constant prices, calendar adjusted and seasonally adjusted, 2021=100 by market, industrial classification (NACE Rev. 2) and month","source":"Statistics Sweden","updated":"2026-09-10T06:00:00Z","note":["Data marked with .. includes classified information or missing data. \r\n  \r\n \r\n  \r\n<B>Methodological changes</B> \r\n  \r\nIn connection with the publishing of April 2015 some methodological changes have introduced, among other a change of index method. The time series have been calculated back to 2000 in order to decrease possible level shifts and breaks in the time series, which have resulted in revisions in some historical series. \r\n  \r\nFrom April 2024, data on order calculated from declared VAT data to the Swedish Tax Agency is used for small and medium-sized enterprises in industrial industries (SNI 07–33). The change is introduced with the ambition to increase quality and streamline the production of functional statistics that describe individual activities in the economy, such as orders in industry. When the new method is introduced, the statistics on orders in industry will be revised as far back in time as possible. In the Statistical Database, values for the periods April 2018 to March 2024 have been revised.  \r\n \r\n  \r\n<B>Revisions</B> \r\n ","2025-02-10: In connection with the publication of the reference month December 2024, the statistics have been corrected for the periods April 2024 to November 2024. This after an error was discovered in the calculation of final statistics for the second and third quarter of 2024 (final statistics for a given month are published one to three months after the first publication for the month depending on the placement within the quarter). The error stems from the model calculation of the turnover of so-called annual filers, i.e. companies that, due to their turnover size, only need to declare VAT annually. The correction affects all industries.","2025-05-09: In connection with the publication of the reference month March 2025, the statistics have been corrected for the industry of chemical, chemical products and pharmaceutical products (NACE 20-21), as well as all aggregates where these sectors are included. The correction concerns the reference month of September 2024.","2025-11-10: In connection with the publication of the reference month September 2025, the statistics have been revised for the industry of paper and paperboard (NACE 17.12) and the industry for motor vehicles (NACE 29). The statistics for the industry of wood and wood products (NACE 16) have been revised for June 2025. The revisions are due to new information received by Statistics Sweden and also apply to all aggregates that include this activity.","2025-12-10: In connection with the publication of the reference month October 2025, the statistics for the industry of chemical, chemical products and pharmaceutical products (NACE 20–21) were revised, as well as all aggregates where these sectors are included. The revision concerns the reference month of June 2025. This is due to new information received by Statistics Sweden.","2026-09-10: In connection with the publication of the reference month July 2026, the statistics for Industry for computer, electronic and optical products (NACE 26) have been revised for the period January 2026 to June 2026. The revisions also affect all aggregates that include the above-mentioned industry. This is due to new information received by Statistics Sweden."],"role":{"time":["Tid"],"metric":["ContentsCode"]},"id":["Marknad","SNI2007","ContentsCode","Tid"],"size":[1,1,1,319],"dimension":{"Marknad":{"label":"market","category":{"index":{"TOTALA":0},"label":{"TOTALA":"total market"}},"extension":{"elimination":true,"eliminationValueCode":"TOTALA","show":"value"}},"SNI2007":{"label":"industrial classification (NACE Rev. 2)","category":{"index":{"B+C":0},"label":{"B+C":"mining, quarrying, manufacturing "}},"e